  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "row-first-run",
      "page": "screens",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2168,
      "w": 620,
      "text": "FIRST RUN — Connect draws what providers.ts actually offers: Spotify halted, YouTube deferred, neither with a live Connect. The mood-only path is the forward action, not a grey skip."
    },
    {
      "id": "row-core-loop",
      "page": "screens",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 3132,
      "w": 660,
      "text": "THE CORE LOOP — the dots carry the emotion you PLACED (gold), the field and CTA carry the FUSED state (violet). Where they disagree, the read card names both voices instead of overriding you. Generate drops the player sheet for a 3px playing hairline so the plate can hold the screen."
    },
    {
      "id": "row-trust",
      "page": "screens",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4096,
      "w": 660,
      "text": "BODY, ARCHIVE, TRUST — Body Battery™ is drawn honest-empty and is genuinely Garmin-only. Daily readiness is NOT — Garmin's Health API supplies no readiness metric, so it reads Not available / No connected source supplies it. Withdraw consent is a RIGHT and takes the neutral border; only account deletion is destructive."
    },
    {
      "id": "row-consent",
      "page": "screens",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 5060,
      "w": 660,
      "text": "CONSENT — four facts pinned above a notice that genuinely scrolls. READ lists only the five categories Health Connect actually requests; the three Garmin-only ones are disclosed separately as covered-but-not-read. Retention is 90 days, per the TTL indexes."
    },
    {
      "id": "sys-note",
      "page": "system",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -110,
      "w": 700,
      "text": "THE SYSTEM — the field's period is now a regulation target (T = 4200 + 2000 × stress), not a division of heart rate. The cardiac-rate beat layer is gone: it repeated at 60000/bpm, which was the mirror the ethic forbids."
    },
    {
      "id": "states-note",
      "page": "states",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -110,
      "w": 700,
      "text": "STATES — two different no-source screens, and the boundary matters. StateNoWatch is the COLD START: nothing paired, no history at all (PulseScreen.tsx:275 isEmpty). Pulse?source=none is LIVE TRANSPORT DROPPED with history intact — the reading still stands, it is just no longer present tense. warmStore.ts:38 makes 'none' the app's cold-start source, so nothing-paired is the first Pulse most people see. The offline banner is mounted app-wide and pushes content down, so Generate is drawn with it in place rather than assuming it away."
    }
  ],
